ng to work during  the virtual learnings  a lot of kids they do need that extra  hands-on  with the teachers one major challenge  the district is facing is how to give  every child access to the internet and a  device  ccsd is trying to acquire 76 thousand  chromebooks by fall  the guide states that schools are  reaching out to families directly to  assess their needs  with all of these changes the district  is offering parents academic  and emotional training opportunities  those will be available in live sessions  and pre-recorded content kate houston  8 news now the chief academic officer  for ccsd will be joining us live later  in this show and we will ask her to  really zero in on the plan  for those ieps and english language  learner students  and as you just heard brian the school  district has ordered some 76  000 chromebooks by the fall as of right  now the district has not said exactly  how many of those  it has received now schools are handing  them out as they get them  we caught up with staff at spring valley  high school where about 1 000 were  needed there  if your child need one needs one excuse  me you've been asked to fill out a  survey  go to the maine school district website  where it inquires about  technology and if you need help with  internet access  also remember to update your contact  information on the infinite campus  now once those students get chromebooks  they'll have to get online and the  school district will consider purchasing  discounted cox connect  internet for about 20 thousand students  they'll be talking about that during the  board meeting this week  ccsd's back to school website also has a  list of businesses supplying hot  spots and as for those wi-fi buses the  district used at the end of last year  they may be deployed on an as-needed  basis  brian about two-thirds of the students  in ccsd get free or reduced  breakfast and lunch for many it's really  the only way they'll get a meal during  the day  here is ccsd's plan 